{
  "abstract": "We present results from a study of high-momentum inclusive hadron production in electron-positron interactions at s=3.8\u00a0and\u00a04.8 GeV. Comparison of the momentum spectra at these energies shows no scaling violation in the region x(=EEbeam)>0.7. At s=4.8 GeV the K\u03c0 ratio for hadrons with momenta >1.1 GeV/c is 0.27\u00b10.08, and the average number of charged hadrons is 3.6\u00b10.3 for those events which have at least one charged hadron with momentum greater than 1.1 GeV/c.",
